{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And you shall say before YHWH your Elohim.</b> Make confession that you have given your tithes." "<b>I have cleared the sacred portion from the house.</b> This is second tithe and fourth-year planting (Sifrei; Ma'aser Sheni 11). And it teaches you that if one delayed his tithes of two years and did not bring them up to Jerusalem, he must bring them up now." "<b>And I have also given it to the Levite.</b> First tithe. <b>Also.</b> To include terumah and first fruits." "<b>And to the stranger, the orphan, and the widow.</b> This is poor man's tithe (ibid.)." "<b>According to all Your commandments.</b> I gave them in their order — I did not precede terumah before first fruits, nor tithe before terumah, nor second before first — for terumah is called רֵאשִׁית, for it is the first taken from produce, and it is written (Exodus 22) ״מְלֵאָתְךָ וְדִמְעֲךָ לֹא תְאַחֵר״ — do not change the order (Sifrei)." "<b>I have not transgressed Your commandments.</b> I did not separate from one species upon a species that is not its kind, nor from the new upon the old (there)." "<b>And I have not forgotten.</b> To bless You on the separation of tithes (Berakhot 40a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:30.295511514Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}